        "original_id": "9f5d9492-4e21-5873-9d69-4df3a3373331",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Turner Field, Centennial Olympic Stadium, Atlanta\n- Organizations: Atlanta Braves\n- Events: 1996 Summer Olympics, 1996 Summer Paralympic Games\n- Topics: stadium conversion, team home venue, baseball seasons\n\nFacts:\n- Centennial Olympic Stadium was an 85,000-seat main stadium for the 1996 Summer Olympic Games and the 1996 Summer Paralympic Games in Atlanta.\n- Turner Field was originally built as Centennial Olympic Stadium in 1996 to serve as the centerpiece of the 1996 Summer Olympics.\n- Turner Field was later converted from Centennial Olympic Stadium into a baseball park to become the new home of the Atlanta Braves.\n- The 2013 Atlanta Braves season was the team's 17th season playing home games at Turner Field, its 48th season in Atlanta, and its 143rd season overall.",
